-- NorthstarIQ — Authoritative Salesforce Lead conversion evidence
--
-- ⚠️ NEW REPRODUCIBILITY ARTIFACT, created 2026-08-27 after the native Lead
-- conversion experiment. It was NOT used in any earlier validation, and it is
-- not historical evidence: it is the query that lets the conversion invariant
-- be re-checked on demand.
--
-- Purpose: separate the two things that are easy to conflate.
--
--   1. SALESFORCE CONVERSION INTEGRITY — did the platform actually convert
--      this Lead? The platform's own answer is IsConverted, and it sets
--      ConvertedDate, ConvertedAccountId and ConvertedContactId in the same
--      transaction. Status is a claim; IsConverted is the fact. Where the two
--      disagree, the claim is wrong.
--
--   2. NORTHSTARIQ BUSINESS POLICY — should an Opportunity exist? Salesforce
--      allows conversion WITHOUT one: the native Convert modal carries a
--      "Don't create an opportunity upon conversion" checkbox, verified on
--      2026-08-27. So a null ConvertedOpportunityId is a valid converted Lead,
--      not a defect, unless NorthstarIQ policy separately requires the
--      Opportunity. Do not fold that requirement into the integrity test.
--
-- Expected on 2026-08-27 against the loaded fixture set: 3 rows, all of them
-- Status = 'Closed - Converted' with IsConverted = false and every Converted*
-- field null. Those three are the deliberate baseline defect that
-- Opportunity Conversion Integrity detects. A row with IsConverted = true is
-- a genuinely converted Lead and should not appear in this result.
--
-- Read-only. Safe to run against any org.

SELECT Id,
       Name,
       Company,
       Status,
       IsConverted,
       ConvertedDate,
       ConvertedAccountId,
       ConvertedContactId,
       ConvertedOpportunityId,
       Lifecycle_Stage_Entered__c
FROM Lead
WHERE Status = 'Closed - Converted'
   OR IsConverted = true
ORDER BY IsConverted DESC, Company
